Hotel Booking Management

Create a class Hotel with the below attributes:

hotelId – int
hotelName – String
dateOfBooking – String (in the format dd-mon-yyyy)
noOfRoomsBooked – int
wifiFacility – String
totalBill – double

The above attributes should be private. Write getters, setters, and a parameterized constructor as required.

Create a class Solution with the main() method.

Implement the following two static methods in the Solution class.

Method 1
noOfRoomsBookedInGivenMonth(Hotel[] hotels, String month)

This method takes:

an array of Hotel objects
a String representing a month

The method should return the total number of rooms booked in the given month.

The month should be obtained from the dateOfBooking attribute (format: dd-mon-yyyy).

If no hotel booking exists for the given month, return 0.

Method 2
searchHotelByWifiOption(Hotel[] hotels, String wifiOption)

This method takes:

an array of Hotel objects
a String representing the WiFi option

The method should return the Hotel object having the second highest totalBill among the hotels whose wifiFacility matches the given WiFi option.

If no hotel with the given WiFi option is found, return null.

Note
No two Hotel objects will have the same hotelId.
No two Hotel objects will have the same totalBill.
The array either contains at least two hotels with the specified WiFi option or none.
All searches should be case-insensitive.

dateOfBooking is stored in the format:

dd-mon-yyyy

Example:

01-Jan-2022
